    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2QDdTfoDxMxaJgd9Y2t9Ap6)_\n\nFollow-up to #472 and #478.\n\n## Merge order\n- Independent; touches only `sp-fetch-inbox.el`, its literate doc and its tests.\n\n## Cause (measured this time)\n- Sia's profile: DEVONthink script 0.15 s, folder scan 0.34 s, merge 0.67 s, **arrange and candidates 11.5 s** for 6296 files. #478 targeted the wrong step.\n- `sp-fetch-inbox--arrange` ran `seq-filter` over all items once per folder, so cost is folders × items.\n- Reproduced in batch Emacs 29.3 on a synthetic tree of 6296 PDFs: 40 folders took 0.35 s, 1500 folders took 5.3 s.\n\n## Changes\n- Group with one pass into a hash-table bucket per folder, keeping the order.\n- Same for the folder counts of the `C-u` / `C-c d` prompt.\n- After the fix, the 1500-folder case takes 0.19 s.\n- Test: 6000 items in 1500 folders arrange in under 1.5 s, folders stay together, newest folder first.\n- Whole `tests/sp-fetch-inbox-test.el` run in batch Emacs: 32 of 32 pass. The `sp-fetch-inbox-prefix-argument-folder-with-spaces` test from #478 was wrong (it expected no picker); fixed.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [ ] `M-x sp-fetch-inbox` with the real inbox: the `arrange and candidates` profile line is well under a second\n- [x] Grouping and order unchanged: newest first, `C-c s` toggles A-Z, `(inbox)` group first in A-Z\n- [ ] `C-c d` lists folders with counts and restricts correctly\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCXyk3bC6YPxjXfvkE)_",
